{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-103038-r4523913","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Black Bean Chili","sourcePageId":103038,"sourceRevision":"4523913","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-15T18:33:27Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Black%20Bean%20Chili&oldid=4523913","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:43.580Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for chili","Category:Recipes using ancho chile","Category:Recipes using black bean","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chipotle chile","Category:Recipes using corn oil","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Slow cooker recipes","Category:Tex-Mex recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"0176278b4a1a649fbbe620a844c920bcb528435c82978f0f5b7c125060b05ced","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Chili recipes|servings=12 persons|time=4 hours|difficulty=3}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:beans|Beans]] | [[Cookbook:Chili|Chili]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 3½ [[Cookbook:cup|cup]]s (8 [[Cookbook:Deciliter|dL]]) dried [[Cookbook:Black Bean|black beans]] \n* 2 [[Cookbook:tablespoon|tablespoon]]s (30 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|mL]]) [[Cookbook:Corn Oil|corn oil]] or other [[Cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:clove|cloves]] [[Cookbook:garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Chipotle Pepper|chipotle]] chile\n* ¼ ancho [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile]]\n* 1 tablespoon (15 mL) [[Cookbook:cumin|cumin]]\n* 1 tablespoon (15 mL) [[Cookbook:paprika|paprika]]\n* 1 tablespoon (15 mL) dried [[Cookbook:oregano|oregano]]\n* ¾ tablespoon (11 mL) sea [[Cookbook:salt|salt]]\n* ⅛ [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] (1 mL) [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* 2 tablespoons (30 mL) wine [[Cookbook:vinegar|vinegar]] (red or white)\n* 1½ cups (350 mL) diced [[Cookbook:tomato|tomato]]es\n* 1½ cups (350 mL) [[Cookbook:tomato|tomato]] puree\n* 4 cups (1 [[Cookbook:Liter|L]]) [[Cookbook:water|water]]\n* [[Cookbook:sour cream|Sour cream]] for [[Cookbook:garnish|garnish]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Place beans in a large pot, add with enough water to cover by 2 [[Cookbook:Inch|inches]] (2.5 cm), and allow to soak overnight. Drain beans and cover again with fresh water. Bring to [[Cookbook:boil|boil]], reduce heat, and [[Cookbook:simmer|simmer]] for 2 hours.\n# Heat the corn oil in a stockpot or other very large pot over medium-high heat. Add the onions and [[Cookbook:saute|sauté]] until tender, about 3 minutes. Add garlic, chipotle and ancho chiles, cumin, paprika, oregano, salt, cayenne, and vinegar, and sauté for 5 to 10 minutes.\n# Add tomatoes, tomato puree, and the water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 10 minutes. Add the beans with their juice. Simmer for 1 hour.\n# Serve with or without sour cream.\n\n[[Category:Slow cooker recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using black bean|Black Bean Chili]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chili|Black Bean Chili]]\n[[Category:Tex-Mex recipes|Black Bean Chili]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|Black Bean Chili]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chipotle chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ancho chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Black Bean Chili","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3½ cups (8 dL) dried black beans","sourceText":"3½ cups (8 dL) dried black beans","amountText":"3½ cups (8 dL) dried black beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tablespoons (30 mL) corn oil or other vegetable oil","sourceText":"2 tablespoons (30 mL) corn oil or other vegetable oil","amountText":"2 tablespoons (30 mL) corn oil or other vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 medium onion, diced","sourceText":"1 medium onion, diced","amountText":"1 medium onion, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 cloves garlic, minced","sourceText":"2 cloves garlic, minced","amountText":"2 cloves garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 chipotle chile","sourceText":"1 chipotle chile","amountText":"1 chipotle chile","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"¼ ancho chile","sourceText":"¼ ancho chile","amountText":"¼ ancho chile","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) cumin","sourceText":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) cumin","amountText":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) cumin","amount":null,"unit":n